sequenceDiagram
    participant TPM as TPM Chip<br/>(hardware)
    participant Agent as SPIRE Agent<br/>(spire-agent pod)
    participant Server as SPIRE Server<br/>(spire-server-0)
    participant DevIDCA as DevID CA<br/>(offline / ConfigMap)
    participant EKCA as EK CA Bundle<br/>(Nuvoton / Infineon)

    Note over Agent: Startup: load DevID material from /etc/spire/

    Agent->>TPM: CreatePrimary(Owner hierarchy, SRKTemplateHighRSA)
    TPM-->>Agent: SRK handle (deterministic — same params = same key)

    Agent->>TPM: Load(SRK, devid.priv, devid.pub)
    TPM-->>Agent: DevID key handle

    Note over Agent,Server: Phase 1 — Proof of Key Possession

    Agent->>Server: AttestationRequest(devid.crt, signed nonce)
    Server->>DevIDCA: Verify devid.crt chain → ipc-cluster DevID CA
    DevIDCA-->>Server: chain valid ✓

    Note over Agent,Server: Phase 2 — Proof of TPM Residency (Credential Activation)

    Server->>TPM: Fetch EK public key (read from EK cert in devid.crt or directly)
    Server->>EKCA: Verify EK cert chain → Nuvoton / Infineon manufacturer CA
    EKCA-->>Server: EK cert valid — hardware is a genuine TPM ✓

    Server->>Server: MakeCredential(EK pub, DevID key name, random secret)
    Note right of Server: Encrypted blob can only be decrypted<br/>by the TPM holding the EK,<br/>and only if the DevID key is loaded<br/>in that same TPM

    Server-->>Agent: CredentialActivation challenge (encrypted blob)

    Agent->>TPM: ActivateCredential(EK handle, DevID handle, blob)
    Note right of TPM: TPM decrypts using EK.<br/>Succeeds only if DevID key<br/>is loaded in this TPM.
    TPM-->>Agent: decrypted secret

    Agent->>Server: Return decrypted secret

    Server->>Server: secret matches → both proofs satisfied

    Note over Agent,Server: Attestation complete

    Server-->>Agent: Node SVID<br/>spiffe://ipc.local/spire/agent/tpm_devid/<sha1>

    Agent->>Agent: Store Node SVID<br/>Open mTLS connection to server<br/>Sync registration entries

    Note over Agent: Agent is now ready to serve<br/>the Workload API on agent.sock
